A timer that fires disarms itself behind the count's back.
The stall in wfi would go on waiting for a timer that will never fire;
the count of armed sources is exactly the armed timers and device Irqs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the count of armed sources is wrong

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -156,3 +156,3 @@
         uint32_t bits = t->bits;
-        timer_set_bits(t, 0);
+        t->bits = 0;
         sched_signal(timer_notification(t), bits);
